.TH enstow 1  "enstow 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
enstow \- Secret\-aware dotfile manager combining stow symlinking with sops/age decryption
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBenstow\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-age\-key\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPACKAGES\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Secret\-aware dotfile manager combining stow symlinking with sops/age decryption
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to configuration file (TOML, YAML, or JSON)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Source directory containing dotfiles
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Target directory to apply dotfiles
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview actions without writing changes to disk
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing target files or differing symlinks
.TP
\fB\-\-age\-key\-file\fR \fI<AGE_KEY_FILE>\fR
Explicit path to age identity key file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPACKAGES\fR]
Dotfile packages to stow or unstow
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
enstow\-apply(1)
Apply dotfiles: symlink regular files and decrypt secret files
.TP
enstow\-restow(1)
Restow dotfiles: clean stale symlinks/secrets and re\-apply
.TP
enstow\-unstow(1)
Unstow dotfiles: remove symlinks and decrypted secret files
.TP
enstow\-encrypt(1)
Encrypt a secret dotfile
.TP
enstow\-edit(1)
Edit an age encrypted secret file interactively
.TP
enstow\-status(1)
Show status of dotfiles and symlinks
.TP
enstow\-man(1)
Generate UNIX roff man page
.TP
enstow\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
